-- ConsumableData.lua
-- CTRBLXAI | Consumable Item Catalog
-- Auto-generated from CTRBLXAI.db consumable_items table.
-- Do not edit manually. Regenerate from database.
--
-- 137 consumable items across 7 categories (20 each except Control 19 - CON-016 Magnetic Snare removed 2026-10-27; Utility 18 - UTI-007 Auto-Key removed 2026-10-26, UTI-012 Recovery Winch removed 2026-10-27):
-- Recovery (REC), Damage (DAM), Control (CON), Support (SUP),
-- Environment (ENV), Deployable (DEP), Utility (UTI)
--
-- numericId ranges: Recovery 201-220, Damage 221-240, Control 241-260,
-- Support 261-280, Environment 281-300, Deployable 301-320, Utility 321-340
--
-- parked = true: DB Status contains PARKED; the game hides the item (not sold, dropped, given to enemies, or equippable). Remove PARKED from Status and regenerate to bring it back.
--
-- pulse* fields (optional; DB consumable_items.Pulse_*): data-driven spec for the
--   PulseScheduler. pulseKind = "heal"|"damage"|"status"|"tileEffect"|"relocate"
--   (tileEffect: create tile effect pulseTileEffect, e.g. "Poison Cloud", on every pulse tile; no direct unit status); pulseAmount (flat or % when
--   pulseAmountKind = "pctMaxHp"; nil for damage = parse "<Element> Power = ..." formula);
--   pulseElement; pulseStatus + pulseStatusCt (nil = status default duration);
--   pulseRadius (Chebyshev, 0 = anchor tile); pulseInterval (CT); pulsePulses (count);
--   pulseOffsetCt (CT before first pulse). pulseRingFalloff (optional; DB Pulse_Ring_Falloff) = array of
--   damage multipliers by Chebyshev ring from the anchor: [1]=centre, [2]=ring 1, [3]=ring 2 (DAM-020 only). pulseNote = design note. Items with a
--   pulseNote but no pulseKind are intentionally deferred - the scheduler must skip them.
--
-- terrainTransforms / terrainTransformMode / terrainSideEffect (optional; DB consumable_items.
--   Terrain_Transforms / Terrain_Transform_Mode / Terrain_Side_Effect). terrainTransforms is a list of
--   {from = {<terrain id>, ...}, to = <terrain id>}; ids are GameConstants.TERRAIN_TYPES keys. For each tile
--   in the item pattern: if GetTerrainId is in a rule's from list, SetTerrainId(x, y, to). Mode "all" =
--   apply every matching rule; "choice" = player picks ONE rule (needs choice UI). terrainSideEffect lines
--   starting "DEFER:" describe clauses the engine should skip for now. DB string form: "A,B>C;D>E".
--
-- tileEffect / tileEffectCt / tileElement (optional; DB consumable_items.Tile_Effect / Tile_Effect_Ct / Tile_Element,
--   added 2026-10-26): tileEffect = existing tile effect created on the pattern tiles for tileEffectCt CT
--   (ENV-005/CON-011 Steam 1600, ENV-001 Oily 1200); tileElement = run the normal element reaction on each tile
--   (ENV-002 Water). Nil on all other items.
--
-- device* / extra pulse* fields (optional; added 2026-10-26, DB consumable_items.Device_* / Pulse_*):
--   summon-kind deployables spawn a non-acting device unit (skips its turns).
--   deviceHpFormula (string, nil = summon profile default HP); deviceLifespanCt (nil = lives until destroyed);
--   deviceAuraRadius / deviceAuraStability / deviceAuraTeleportLock (boolean).
--   deviceInterceptCount (integer; DB Device_Intercept_Count, added 2026-10-27): DEP-018 blocks this many hostile ranged
--   attacks (projectiles) aimed at a unit within deviceAuraRadius; blocked hit deals nothing; max 1 block per attack/skill use;
--   afterwards the device stays as an inert 3-hit device. Omitted when nil.
--   deviceAuraWeatherShield (boolean; DB Device_Aura_Weather_Shield 0/1, added 2026-10-27): units within deviceAuraRadius
--   ignore current weather (no new weather statuses, weather damage or weather element change) except locked weather
--   effects (e.g. Snow Storm locked Frozen). DEP-014 only. Omitted when false/nil.
--   deviceAuraWardMult (number; DB Device_Aura_Ward_Mult, added 2026-10-26): incoming DIRECT damage multiplier of the
--   element picked on placement, for same-side units in deviceAuraRadius (DEP-013 0.8). Totals with Elemental Ward status;
--   same-element totems do not stack (strongest applies). Omitted when nil.
--   pulseAmountFormula (ASCII formula string); pulseTargetMode = "all"|"nearest"|"lowestHp";
--   pulseRequiresLoS (boolean); pulseRecipients = "enemies"|"allies";
--   pulseAnchor = "device" (pulses follow the device, stop when it dies; nil = fixed tile).
--   pulseAnchor = "target" (added 2026-10-27; REC-007/REC-008): the pulse follows the target unit and stops if it dies.
--   pulseTargetMode = "anchor" (added 2026-10-27): only the anchor unit itself is affected (no radius search).
--   pulseStatus / pulseStatusCt: CON-002 Dazzle Beacon is a bodiless tile status pulse (Blind 800 CT), no deployKind.
--   deviceAuraGuardBonus (number; DB Device_Aura_Guard_Bonus, added 2026-10-27): allies within deviceAuraRadius get this
--   much extra Guard (0.05 = +5 percentage points) while Guarding. SUP-011 Guardian Standard only. Omitted when nil.
--   deviceAuraTaunt (boolean; DB Device_Aura_Taunt 0/1, added 2026-10-27): enemies within deviceAuraRadius get the Taunted
--   status with the device as taunter (only basic attacks / Debuff / Direct Damage skills on it); ends on leaving the area,
--   re-applied while inside. CON-018 Taunt Beacon only. Omitted when false/nil.
--   Device damage pulses follow normal damage rules (Defense, elements, wards; project_rules 177).
--
-- appliesStatus (optional): maps DB column consumable_items.Applies_Status.
-- Present only on Support items that apply a single buff/debuff status; the
-- item effect engine reads it to resolve which status to apply. Absent when null.
--
-- statusRecipients (optional): maps DB column consumable_items.Status_Recipients. "all" = the
-- area-status handler applies appliesStatus to every unit on the AOE tiles regardless of side
-- (neutral zone). Absent/nil = default side rules. Currently only CON-015 Gravity Anchor.
--
-- pulseFireImmediate (optional boolean; DB consumable_items.Pulse_Fire_Immediate 0/1, added 2026-10-26): true = fire the
--   first pulse on placement, then every pulseInterval. Omitted when NULL/0. pulseKind "reveal" (DEP-011/012) = removes
--   Hide from every unit in pulseRadius (both sides; pulseRecipients "all") and reveals hidden objects there.
--
-- deployKind / deployRef / deployParams / deployNote (Deployable items only):
--   Tells the item effect engine HOW each Deployable's runtime behaviour is driven,
--   so no hardcoded item->type map is needed in source. Maps DB columns
--   consumable_items.Deploy_Kind / Deploy_Ref / Deploy_Params / Deploy_Note.
--   deployKind = "summon" -> deployRef is a summon profile (Turret/Decoy/Mender/WardTotem),
--     spawned via EnemyGenerator.SpawnSummon using the numbers in deployParams.
--   deployKind = "object" -> deployRef is an ObjectData archetype placed via
--     ObjectEffectService.PlaceObjectInstance; deployParams overrides its stats.
--   deployKind = "defer" -> deployRef is a short reason: the runtime system this item
--     needs does not exist yet (placement+durability foundation still applies).
--   deployParams carries the authored numbers (HP, power, pulses, durations) for the
--     spawner; deployNote records deltas vs the reused profile/archetype and flags.

